---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { EXAMPLES } from "../../examples";
---
<Base title="Repair completion report examples" description="Five fictional repairs written up as Open Repair Records: a normal repair, a temporary fix, no reply, a reopened job and a visit with no access." section="examples">
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Examples</p>
    <h1>Repair completion report examples</h1>
    <p class="lead">Five fictional repairs, each written up as a complete repair completion report. Each is a record you can read, print, download as JSON or open in the builder. All names, companies and addresses are invented.</p>
    <p style="max-width:46rem">
      Each example shows one situation that ordinary completion reports handle badly: a repair the resident confirms,
      a temporary fix with work still to do, a resident who never answers, a fault that comes back after the job was
      closed, and a visit where nobody let the contractor in. Read them to see how each part of the record is filled
      in, then open one in the builder and change it into your own job.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:28px">
      {EXAMPLES.map((e, i) => (
        <a class="card card-link" href={`/examples/${e.slug}/`}>
          <div class="part-num">{i + 1}</div>
          <h2 class="card-h">{e.name}</h2>
          <p class="muted">{e.lesson}</p>
          <span class="more">See the report →</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
